Hi All,

I am confused about how renaming through select works, which may just be because I am new to R and dplyr (many thanks, by the way!) and don't understand it yet.

I am using version 0.2 of dplyr

The behavior that appears inconsistent is:

names( select(iris, starts_with("P"), sepal.wid = Sepal.Width))
[1] "Petal.Length" "Petal.Width"  "sepal.wid"

This works as expected.

names( select(iris, starts_with("S"), sepal.wid = Sepal.Width))
[1] "Sepal.Length" "Sepal.Width"  "Species"

I expected Sepal.Width to be renamed to sepal.wid

> names( select(iris, -matches("^P"), sepal.wid = Sepal.Width))
[1] "sepal.wid"

I expect this to return the same thing as the previous, with Sepal.Width renamed to sepal.wid.

Zooming out, I would expect selecting to be separate from renaming, as in:

iris %>% select(starts_with("S")) %>% rename(sepal.wid = Sepal.Width)

but I am not aware of a rename function.

Thank you,
Ryan

