>
> I am confused about how renaming through select works, which may just be
> because I am new to R and dplyr (many thanks, by the way!) and don't
> understand it yet.
>
> I am using version 0.2 of dplyr
>
> The behavior that appears inconsistent is:
>
> names( select(iris, starts_with("P"), sepal.wid = Sepal.Width))
> [1] "Petal.Length" "Petal.Width"  "sepal.wid"
>
> This works as expected.
>
> names( select(iris, starts_with("S"), sepal.wid = Sepal.Width))
> [1] "Sepal.Length" "Sepal.Width"  "Species"
>
> I expected Sepal.Width to be renamed to sepal.wid

Here's a slightly simpler variation to show you what's going on:

names(select(iris, Species, Species))
names(select(iris, x = Species, Species))
names(select(iris, x = Species, y = Species))
names(select(iris, Species, y = Species))

i.e. select() uses the name associated with the variable the _first_
time you mention it. That seems a reasonable approach to me.

Hadley

